## LCOH Off-Grid Electricity Run — Spec v1.4.0 Complete

**Outputs written to `./outputs/`:**
| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `lcoh_results.csv` | 3,591 rows — 33 columns including new `bnef_data_source`, `bnef_year_used`, `lcoh_confidence` |
| `price_sources_log.csv` | 5,277 price lookup records |
| `cross_run_comparison.csv` | 860 flagged cross-run anomalies |
| `assumptions_log.md` | Full assumption register with sources (spec v1.4.0) |
| `method_summary.md` | Formulas, BNEF coverage, confidence/plausibility tables |
| `verification_report.md` | Checklist + §9.2.1 plausibility check + §9.2.3 cross-run |

**Key v1.3.1 → v1.4.0 corrections:**
- **Critical methodology fix:** Heat battery now uses **PV-only electricity** (no BESS) instead of PV+BESS. HB avg LCOH dropped from ~157.5 to **45.2 EUR/MWh_th** — this is the correct value since the heat battery itself is the storage device.
- Added `bnef_data_source`, `bnef_year_used`, `lcoh_confidence` columns per spec §5.1.3, §6.8
- BNEF year mapping corrected to explicit rule (≤2027 → 2025; ≥2028 → 2030)
- A15 widened to 50% per spec note
- Literature plausibility check (§9.2.1) and cross-run comparison (§9.2.3) added

**Key results (1,759 facilities with LCOH computed):**
- Heat battery is least-cost for **1,448 facilities** (avg 45.2 EUR/MWh_th vs gas avg 80.7) — driven by cheap off-grid PV (~38–47 EUR/MWh for most EU countries, no BESS needed)
- HIGH confidence = 0 (all analysis years are 2017–2022, all proxied to BNEF 2025; MEDIUM is the practical maximum)
- 103 gas LCOH outliers (>130 EUR/MWh_th), 268 HB outliers (<40 EUR/MWh_th mostly southern EU), 136 electricity LCOE outliers (GBR PV+BESS just over 160 USD/MWh threshold)[2026-06-08T17:51:55Z] PHASE_1_START: Loading BNEF off-grid electricity + Eurostat gas
